  "matching": "Patterns match with matchesStaple() from src/lib/units.ts — a pattern hits when its words appear as consecutive whole words in the name, so \"corn\" does not claim \"cornstarch\" and \"coconut milk\" does not get claimed by \"milk\". The MOST SPECIFIC pattern wins across every aisle, counted in words then characters, which is what puts coconut milk in the tins rather than the dairy case. \"except\" takes something back out.",
